{"name":"Caribbean","hex":"#caf0e5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Caribbean","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the sea and region of the western Atlantic bounded by South America, Central America, and the islands of the West Indies (such as Cuba and Hispaniola)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person native to the Caribbean region","A member of the Amerindian tribes that inhabited the Caribbean region before the arrival of the Europeans"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Caribbean"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean","wikidata":"Q664609"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/1280px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg/500px-Atlantic_continents_at_night_by_VIIRS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":